From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew <andrew@localhost>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 06:55:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] module-droid-card: guard park_profile against a null
 am->source

Ported from the jb2q-fork patch of the same name in the recipe next to
this one - park_profile() has been byte-for-byte identical between the
two forks since before the Android-11 split, this bug included.

If the Android input stream failed to open (e.g. the HAL rejected the
open call), pa_droid_source_new() returns NULL and am->source is left
NULL with no error propagated - init_profile() and update_profile()
don't check it either. park_profile() (called whenever the active card
profile is switched away from) then unconditionally calls
pa_source_set_port(am->source, ...) - a PulseAudio core API that hard
asserts on a null source, aborting the whole daemon.

Originally found and fixed against the jb2q fork (2026-09-04) while
tracking down a real SIGABRT on this project's own device, before
discovering (2026-09-11) that jb2q is the wrong generation for that
device's Android 14 vendor in the first place - see the SUMMARY of
pulseaudio-modules-droid_git.bb. Porting the same one-line guard here
so the correct-generation build carries it too.

The output/sink side already only sets a port for primary mappings and
happens to always succeed in practice; guard the input/source side the
same way sink already implicitly is, by additionally requiring
am->source to be non-null before touching it.

Signed-off-by: Andrew <andrew@localhost>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/droid/module-droid-card.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/droid/module-droid-card.c b/src/droid/module-droid-card.c
--- a/src/droid/module-droid-card.c
+++ b/src/droid/module-droid-card.c
@@ -445,7 +445,7 @@ static void park_profile(pa_droid_profile *dp) {
 
     /* Virtual profiles don't have input mappings. */
     if ((am = dp->input_mapping)) {
-        if (pa_droid_mapping_is_primary(am))
+        if (pa_droid_mapping_is_primary(am) && am->source)
             pa_source_set_port(am->source, PA_DROID_INPUT_PARKING, false);
     };
 }
